Build order for Version 1

Replace auth-heavy files with this scaffold.

Keep frontend simple for now: remove login, remove claims of LSTM, rename to assistant-guided strategy builder.

Run backend first with the temporary YFinanceProvider.

Test /api/assistant/suggest, /api/backtest, /api/live-chart/{ticker}.

After backend is stable, implement UpstoxProvider in market_data.py.

Then update dashboard.js to use assistant suggestion payloads and render rationale + overlays.

Immediate tasks you must do next

Put dashboard.html, dashboard.js, app.js, unified-theme.css in the same folder as main.py if serving UI from backend.

Remove all token/auth code from frontend.

Change any 'LSTM' label to 'Strategy Assistant' or 'Projection'.

Add a simple assistant form that posts to /api/assistant/suggest.

When suggestion is returned, autofill backtest parameters.

Backtest using /api/backtest/from-assistant or /api/backtest.

Upstox integration plan

Add access token env handling.

Build instrument lookup map.

Implement get_history using official candle endpoint.

Implement get_live_snapshot with websocket stream aggregation.

Keep the same returned OHLCV structure so UI/backtester code does not change.

Why this order

Schema first keeps the assistant, UI, and backtester aligned.

Provider abstraction prevents lock-in to yfinance.

Backtester cleanup now avoids reworking metrics later.

Live chart can evolve independently once provider output is normalized.